title: Ovarian function suppression in breast cancer
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Role:'' Add ovarian function suppression (OFS) to endocrine therapy for higher-risk premenopausal hormone receptor-positive early breast cancer; tamoxifen alone suits low-risk disease ([[SOFT/TEXT|SOFT and TEXT - Adjuvant endocrine therapy]]).
* ''Methods:'' Reversible gonadotropin-releasing hormone agonists (goserelin/leuprolide) or permanent bilateral oophorectomy.
* ''Pearl:'' Aromatase inhibitors require confirmed ovarian suppression; chemotherapy-induced amenorrhea does not establish menopause.
* ''Toxicity:'' Menopausal symptoms, sexual dysfunction, bone loss.

Sources: [[NCI|https://www.cancer.gov/types/breast/treatment/hormone-therapy]]; ASCO-SEP 2026, Breast Cancer, p. 462; NCCN Breast Cancer v6.2026, BINV-K 2/4; Discussion MS-36–37.
